docs/adr/0021-prod-validation-security-review-reaches-past-the-diff.md:20:- D3 enforcement: `delivery_gate.py check` at the merge ask plus the command in the worker's acceptance script, no FO word changed (chosen); an FO step in `### validation` — not chosen: about 25 words in a file 16 words under budget
docs/adr/0021-prod-validation-security-review-reaches-past-the-diff.md:25:A prod task's validation worker dispatches the reviewer once with the Reach brief, saves the report as `security/validation-<N>.yaml`, writes `Security review (validation): <path> at <head>` and one `Security finding (validation <N>) <n>:` line per finding (`Material`, `declined` on MEDIUM or LOW only, or `Needs decision`). `validation_security.py`, called from `delivery_gate.py check`, refuses a prod task with no review, a `not run` review, a review at any head but the dispatched one the PR head equals, a profile line it cannot read as poc, pilot or prod, a repeated finding line, a report that is not a `tob_security_review` report, a finding with no line, a declined HIGH or CRITICAL, or an open Material finding. A reply with no report is saved, recorded as `not run: reviewer returned no report (<model>)`, and holds the stage, at ideation and at validation.
docs/adr/0023-a-delivery-gate-question-may-carry-the-merge-of-the-validated-head.md:11:Measured on batch 2 (2026-10-17 to 10-19): the Captain gave FO 22 answers to 63 asks; 5 were merge asks outside a gate message and 4 were procedural, one of them a worktree cleanup. 20 of the 22 accepted FO's recommendation as stated, but several came with a question of his first, so acceptance is not evidence for delegating. A written rule could settle at most 2 of the 22: the standalone merge ask of a task PR and the removal of its clean worktree. The other 20 stay his under ADR 0011, README step 4, ADR 0009, his own rulings or the permission check. `delivery_gate.py check` already holds the merge on head, CI, draft, base and file list.
docs/adr/0023-a-delivery-gate-question-may-carry-the-merge-of-the-validated-head.md:15:**Words:** 「照建議」 — Captain, 2026-10-19, chat, approving the four batch-3 ideation gates presented together. The captain-question-load gate question read: "Approve the design and enter implementation as Pilot? Approving accepts D1 (land a Delivery authority sentence that lets a delivery gate question carry the merge of the validated head and the cleanup of its worktree, with 'unless he says he merges' as the opt-out, plus delivery_gate.py's last line saying 'merge this head if the approved question named the merge, else ask', and an ADR that his approval of such a question is his answer), D2 (learning PRs and the Release PR are still asked one at a time), and FO's implementation order below." When the implementation worker's edit of the Delivery authority wording was refused by the permission check, he added, in chat, 「授權修改 Delivery authority 合併措辭，照 D1 設計。但我要你明確跟我說，當我同意/核准驗證關卡時，等於授權你也合併 PR，除非我有顧慮暫時不合併。但這裡必須要硬前提，ＰＲ 必須是 ready 狀態，合理嗎？」 (Captain amendment 1 in the task file).
docs/adr/0023-a-delivery-gate-question-may-carry-the-merge-of-the-validated-head.md:18:- D1 land one Delivery authority sentence and the new text of the last `next:` line of `delivery_gate.py`: when FO's delivery gate question names the merge of the head `delivery_gate.py check` passes and the removal of its clean, pushed worktree, his approval of that question is his answer to both asks, unless he says he merges himself or holds the merge (chosen); keep asking for the merge and the cleanup one at a time — not chosen, it leaves 22 answers at 22
docs/adr/0023-a-delivery-gate-question-may-carry-the-merge-of-the-validated-head.md:23:An approval that says to wait, not to merge yet, or that he has a concern holds the merge, as Captain amendment 1 reserves (「除非我有顧慮暫時不合併」); FO then asks as today. The README sentence is net zero words (the cut sentence defines "green", which `pr_watch.py` and `delivery_gate.py` already enforce). The `ASK` line prints text only: the script reads no question and decides nothing, so the one-bit grant (the approved question said so) stays with FO and the README. ADR 0011's never-delegated list is unchanged because he is still asked, in the delivery question.
docs/adr/0023-a-delivery-gate-question-may-carry-the-merge-of-the-validated-head.md:27:One standalone merge ask and the worktree cleanup ask are removed for a task whose delivery question named them. The merge still waits for `delivery_gate.py check` to exit 0, and the Captain's hard precondition, a PR that is ready and not a draft, is already a hold there (a draft PR exits 1). Worse: a quick approval is no longer followed by a pause before FO merges, so a Material change he would have caught at a second ask has one fewer chance; the head, CI and base checks still run. If FO omits the sentence from the question, the rule fails safe: he is asked again, as today. Nothing checks that a merged PR's approved question named the merge; that check would belong to `fo-write-checks`. The last `next:` line grows from 7 to 25 words at the merge ask. Reopen if a merge lands on an approval whose question did not name it, or if batch 3 still shows a standalone merge ask for a task whose question carried the sentence.
docs/adr/0024-chat-only-fo-rules-are-listed-not-judged.md:11:The observer reports on six batch-2 tasks marked 18 rows `can't tell`, naming 17 FO rules in 40 rule-report pairs. Each row was judged by one question: who or what can see the evidence, and does anyone need it later. 10 pairs are readable from state (`design_surfaces.py check` replayed at the task-file sha a briefing binds; `merge/ask-<N>.json`, written by `delivery_gate.py check` since 0.25.0). 4 are held by FO alone and no one else sees them (the sufficiency and necessity confirmation before a merge ask). 16 are witnessed only by the Captain's chat or by a shell run that leaves no record. 10 are not chat-only and stay as they are or go to `fo-write-checks` and `captain-question-load`. Replaying `design_surfaces.py check` over history exits 1 in 11 of 82 runs for a section the task's gate did not yet need, which is ADR 0017's reason a law over history is red by age; ADR 0014 already accepts that `workflow_checkout.py` is prose-enforced.
docs/adr/0024-chat-only-fo-rules-are-listed-not-judged.md:15:**Words:** 「照建議」 — Captain, 2026-10-19, chat, approving the four batch-3 ideation gates presented together. This task's gate question read: "Approving accepts D1 (the observer stops judging the rules only chat can show: the acceptance steps in full, the package and checkout runs, answering a Captain question, the --names run, the four-field assessment, while the rest are read from state or recorded), D2 (Sufficiency: and Necessity: clauses in the delivery gate text, held by delivery_gate.py), D3 (the acceptance steps shown in full stay chat-only), and FO's implementation order below."
docs/adr/0024-chat-only-fo-rules-are-listed-not-judged.md:19:- D2 `delivery_gate.py` holds a merge ask whose text has no `Sufficiency:` or `Necessity:` clause and saves both in `ask-<N>.json` (chosen); list the confirmation as not judged — not chosen, no one but FO sees it
docs/adr/0024-chat-only-fo-rules-are-listed-not-judged.md:28:The observer stops reporting 16 of the 40 pairs and reads 10 more from state; a first merge ask without both clauses holds once and the hold line names what to add, and an adopter meets that hold at its first ask after a plugin update. `delivery_gate.py` checks that a clause is present, not that it is true, so `Necessity: yes` passes. Worse: an FO that shortens the acceptance steps or skips `workflow_checkout.py` leaves nothing the observer can show, so only the Captain's attention and the script's own hold catch it. Reopen if an observer report or the Captain finds a listed rule broken with nothing in state or chat to show it, if a gate is found presented where `design_surfaces.py check` exits 1 at its bound sha, or if Spacedock gains a pre-dispatch hook (ADR 0014).
docs/adr/0025-a-declined-item-carries-a-bracketed-reason-and-a-reserved-adr-lands-or-is-released.md:15:**Words:** 「照建議」 — Captain, 2026-10-19, chat, approving the four batch-3 ideation gates presented together. The fo-write-checks gate question read: "Approve the design and enter implementation as Pilot? Approving accepts D1 (every declined item in a delivery gate summary carries a bracketed reason, held by delivery_gate.py), D2 (a reserved ADR must exist at the PR head before the merge ask; FO lands the file or deletes the reserved line), and FO's implementation order below." The task design recommended A for D1 (`<class>, <finding> (<reason>)`, enforced as a hold at `delivery_gate.py check`) and no parked form for D2.
docs/adr/0025-a-declined-item-carries-a-bracketed-reason-and-a-reserved-adr-lands-or-is-released.md:18:- D1 A: each declined item in the merge-ask text carries a bracket of two or more words, and `delivery_gate.py check` holds the ask without one (chosen); B bracket or `because`, C a dash form, D leave it to the observer — not chosen (C fails every legacy summary; D leaves reasons unseen until archive)
docs/adr/0026-role-calls-are-owed-on-counts-read-from-task-records-and-a-dated-call-clears-them.md:33:Amended 2026-10-22 (Captain: 「可以」 at the ideation gate of the task `merge-ask-holds-missing-clauses`, narrowing it to this one hold; 「按建議**不算**」 on D2): `delivery_gate.py check` runs `role_triggers.py` on the task folder and stem, without `--review-rounds`, and holds the merge ask while the committed task owes a chief-engineer call (four repair passes) or an engineering-reviewer call (a replacing amendment): exit 1 adds one problem line and the script's `next:` lines, exit 2 holds with its message (「可以」). Review rounds do not hold the ask; idle still prints that call (「按建議不算」). The script reads the task as committed, so an amendment not yet state-committed is not seen and a call not yet state-committed does not clear. "Told once per task and role" above still describes the idle line; a skipped call now also refuses the merge ask until the call or a dated waiver is committed.
docs/adr/0027-fo-write-rules-are-checked-by-the-script-fo-runs-at-the-write.md:11:The batch-3 observers found four FO-write rules broken days after the write: a Captain ruling recorded before the question it settles (delivery-gate-settles-skipped-checks), a two-part finding declined with one part's reason (chat-only-evidence-observer-blind, special-role-calls-fire-when-needed), a Captain scope change after the backlog gate kept outside `## Captain amendments` (special-role-calls-fire-when-needed), and Release PR #672 merged on the approval of #682 (3m50s later, no task, no `delivery_gate.py` run). Spacedock 0.27.2 runs nothing when FO writes a task file, so each check sits at a script FO is already told to run (ADR 0014: prose-enforced until Spacedock gains a pre-write hook).
docs/adr/0027-fo-write-rules-are-checked-by-the-script-fo-runs-at-the-write.md:35:- Rule 4 here is a sentence FO reads. No script checks that an approved question named the merge, so a merge FO makes without running `delivery_gate.py check`, and any merge of a PR with no task (the Release PR, a learning PR), has no check. The premise is the settings read above; it holds for that machine on that date.
docs/adr/0036-a-reserved-adr-may-land-on-a-named-sibling-pr-of-the-same-task.md:11:ADR 0025 D2 holds the merge ask while a reserved `ADR: NNNN` has no `<adr-path>/NNNN-*.md` at the PR head. A task that delivers a plugin and the package that consumes it through two PRs (new-work-starts-from-a-story-map, #704 and #705) reserved its ADR on one of them; `delivery_gate.py check` held the ask for the other, saved no record for it, and the Captain merged #704 after FO asked in chat. Spacedock 0.27.3 tracks one `pr:` string and one `pr-merge:N` sentinel per task, so the second PR is outside its tracking either way. One of the 141 task files here delivered through two PRs (read 2026-10-25).
docs/adr/0036-a-reserved-adr-may-land-on-a-named-sibling-pr-of-the-same-task.md:18:- A: `delivery_gate.py check` takes a repeatable `--sibling-pr owner/repo#N`; a reserved ADR missing at this PR head passes when a named sibling is not closed, its head is a `Candidate:` line of the newest validation record, and the ADR directory at that head lists the number (chosen)
